{"id": "1b33260b-e234-4508-b3c7-63f63ac27094", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit the CloudTrail setup in account 012345678901. That covers trails, event selectors, and the Insights, logging, and delivery settings. I'm starting that now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_ClvuATbffzNKmLPfs1UGHs", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Produce an audit-grade, read-only inventory of the CloudTrail configuration in AWS account 012345678901, stating exactly what IS and IS NOT being captured.",
  "context": "The user's auditors need an exact picture of CloudTrail coverage. Home region of the agent space is us-east-1, but check ALL enabled regions (use ec2 describe_regions to enumerate) since trails may be regional, and multi-region trails/organization trails can be homed elsewhere. Read-only only; make no changes. If CloudTrail calls via use_aws are blocked, say so explicitly and use whatever alternative route is available (e.g. the CloudTrail tooling enabled by your skill, S3/CloudWatch Logs/Config/EventBridge evidence) and clearly flag what could NOT be verified rather than guessing.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901", "all enabled regions"],
  "criteria": "For every trail (include shadow trails, organization trails, and CloudTrail Lake event data stores / channels): name, ARN, home region, IsMultiRegionTrail, IsOrganizationTrail, IncludeGlobalServiceEvents, status via get_trail_status (IsLogging, latest delivery time/errors, latest digest delivery, StartLoggingTime/StopLoggingTime), log file validation (digest) enabled, KMS encryption key, S3 bucket + prefix, CloudWatch Logs log group/role, SNS topic. Event selectors: classic vs advanced event selectors via get_event_selectors; management events (read/write, ExcludeManagementEventSources e.g. kms.amazonaws.com / rdsdata), data events (which resource types e.g. S3 objects, Lambda, DynamoDB, etc., and which ARNs/buckets, read/write), network activity events, and Insights selectors (ApiCallRateInsight / ApiErrorRateInsight). Also: whether any region has NO trail coverage; whether any trail is stopped/not logging; S3 destination bucket checks (public access block, versioning, MFA delete, object lock, lifecycle/retention, bucket policy allowing cloudtrail, access logging) ; CloudTrail Lake event data stores (retention, termination protection, selectors); CloudWatch alarms/metric filters on CloudTrail log groups if present; any recent changes to trails (StopLogging, UpdateTrail, PutEventSelectors, DeleteTrail) in the last 90 days if you can verify. Then explicitly derive a 'NOT captured' list: e.g. S3 data events on which buckets/all buckets, Lambda data events, DynamoDB/other data event types, uncovered regions, excluded management event sources, read-only vs write-only gaps, no Insights, no log validation, no CW Logs integration, etc. Return a structured, concise report: (1) trail inventory table, (2) captured, (3) NOT captured / gaps, (4) findings with severity, (5) anything unverifiable and why."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trails, selectors and coverage across regions"}], "created_at": null}

